  "decision_needed": [
    {
      "question": "The Care Center's 'Loss on Sale of Assets' (924,340) is a nonoperating expense on the revenue/expense statement (p6), but the cash flow statement (p7) shows the same amount as 'Purchase of Fixed Assets'. Should it stay a business-type disbursement or move to business_type.adjustments as a non-cash item?",
      "amount": 924340,
      "recorded_as": "business-type disbursement, category other (review), included in computed business-type disbursements 7,063,816",
      "source_page": 6
    }
  ],
  "notes": "GAAP basis (modified accrual statements). Governmental receipts/disbursements from Statement of Revenues, Expenditures and Changes in Fund Balances, Total Governmental Funds column (p4). Business-type from Statement of Revenues, Expenses and Changes in Fund Net Position, Totals column (p6); no single printed total, so reported business-type totals are computed (operating + nonoperating items). Business-type G&A and depreciation split by the printed fund columns (Rescue Squad public safety, Water/Sewer/Solid Waste utilities, Care Center hospital/health care). Interest expense and loss on sale of assets are nonoperating expenses recorded as disbursements; transfers out (equity) of 2,039,991 from the Care Center matches the General Fund equity transfer in of 2,039,991 (cross-check done; both recorded as transfers). Roll-forwards: governmental 1,299,518 + 1,363,506 - 1,479,876 + 2,039,991 = 3,223,139; business-type 5,991,311 + 5,951,079 - 7,063,816 - 2,039,991 = 2,838,583. Tax types not broken out anywhere in the trimmed pages, so Taxes kept as taxes (unlabeled). ending_cash = Cash and cash equivalents, Total Governmental Funds balance sheet (p3); beginning cash not shown. Balance sheet uses the government-wide Total column (p1). Detail: General Fund lines come from the General Fund combining statement by department column (p13: General, Library, Community Center, Fire Department, Parks, Cemetery; added by the v7 re-trim), which ties to the General column of the governmental funds statement (p4: revenues 531,588, expenditures 784,180). It is more detailed than the budgetary-basis General Fund budget schedule (p8: receipts 529,001, disbursements 784,180; Community Development budget 706,215 with no actual), so the budget schedule's lines are no longer recorded (no double counting) and the department lines carry no budget_final. Street and Debt Service detail come from the budgetary-basis budget-vs-actual schedules (p10, p11), whose actuals differ slightly from the GAAP statements (reconciliation p9: General 1,784,812 budgetary to 1,787,399 GAAP). Nonmajor governmental funds (Economic Development, Keno, Website Development, ARPA, 1999 Housing Rehab Loan) are recorded per fund from the combining statement (p12, added by the v7 re-trim); its Keno fund 'Miscellaneous' 32,114 is categorized keno/lottery from the fund name (the Keno fund's only non-interest revenue; review). Trimmed p2 (Statement of Activities, added by the v7 re-trim) shows Taxes only as 'Taxes - Levied for general purposes' 679,270, so tax types are still not broken out. The p9 reconciliation page and no proprietary budget schedules are included. Trimmed pages are a subset of the 47-page report. proprietary noncapital_financing not shown in cash flow statement. Read pages 1-13 of 13"
}